  "brief_rationale": "Trajectory begins with a strong safety-first message (RC1 red flags and RC3 safe boundaries) and progressively discovers medication details via workspace queries and phone calls. The model directly addresses the misconception that prior omeprazole non-response means all acid-suppression should be stopped, and recognizes the gastric malignancy context (RC2). It identifies hypertension medication uncertainty (RC2 satisfied), obtains a concrete next-step plan with follow-up ownership, monitoring, and fallback (RC5, RC6), and delivers a bounded closure with explicit residual risks and teach-back receipt (HO4 fully completed). No serious or minor in-chain error is found; all RCs are met. Three high-order points (HO1, HO2, HO4) were triggered and fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact, while HO3 received partial navigation of real-world barriers. This meets Strong criteria and exceeds the minimum required for two HOs to reach Perfect, but HO3 is only partially completed, so Perfect is not achieved. Grade 4 is the correct boundary.",
